The paper is clearly above DualRes and Pivoticl (which scored 2.5 and 1.3). It has a genuine conceptual contribution and is clearly motivated, unlike those papers. It falls below Mirror Flow Matching (5.3) and MuLO (5.0), which both had more rigorous theoretical treatments and broader experiments. It is close to AReUReDi (4.0, Reject), perhaps slightly above due to the cleaner conceptual insight and clearer problem framing.

