## Comparative Assessment

### Paper Summary
The paper proposes a compositional meta-learning framework that learns a probabilistic generative model of tasks, separating within-module dynamics (module RNNs = "syllables") from between-module transition statistics (gating RNN = "grammar"). New tasks are solved via particle filtering (inference), not gradient updates. Validated on two synthetic domains — abstract rule-learning and motor control.

### Dimension-by-Dimension Analysis

