### Scoring Rationale

The paper occupies a space between SURE (4.4) and µLO (5.0). Key positives: principled probabilistic formulation, convincing gating ablation, length generalization (4×), full code/reproducibility. Key negatives: evaluation limited to specially-designed synthetic tasks, no comparison to modern in-context learning or transformer-based meta-learning, particle count sensitivity unanalyzed, sparse feedback only qualitatively demonstrated.

The paper is a credible proof-of-concept that makes a genuinely interesting algorithmic contribution, but its empirical claims cannot be evaluated against the field's state of the art. This is a stronger issue than in µLO (which at least crosses multiple architecture families), placing this paper at the lower edge of the 5.0 band — around **4.8**.

