The most apt comparison is just below the unlearning paper—the causal-intervention flaw is more fundamental (it's the paper's *raison d'être*) than the unlearning paper's metric design flaw (which is the secondary contribution, not the core), and the CoT SFT paradox is an unexplained empirical contradiction at the heart of the two-stage design.

